## How to write a good CHANGELOG entry

- One line per change. If you need more than three lines, you are describing two changes — split them.
- Reference the atomic prompt (if any) by its ID: `(prompt: 0007-add-google-login)`.
- Reference the commit short SHA if known.
- Prefer past tense ("Added Google login") over imperative ("Add Google login") — this is history, not instructions.
- When a feature is removed, also delete it from `STATE.md`. CHANGELOG keeps the memory; STATE keeps the truth.

